From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: GC write-back skip, the collector leaves an image whose write-back would grow the swizzle scratch (EDEN_UP_GC_WRITEBACK_SKIP)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (gc-scratch job), after waveydude's two GPUBack std::bad_alloc
deaths (32 MiB new[] in SwizzleImage under RunGarbageCollector). Gated by
EDEN_UP_GC_WRITEBACK_SKIP (exact 1, live, Id GcWritebackSkip, not armed); off by default. On: a
collector candidate (and RefusalDownloadEvict's choice) whose block-linear write-back is split and
larger than the scratch (and at least 256 KiB) stays for now, still GPU-written and registered.
EDEN_UP_GC_WRITEBACK_SKIP_VERIFY=1 (boot) only checks the prediction. EDEN_TEST_GC_WRITEBACK_STARVE=1
(boot, test aid) runs the write-back in the front's heap wait scope. 10 s line while on:
"EDEN_UP_GC_WRITEBACK_SKIP:". Needs the front change in headless/vulkan_gc_downloads.inc (same
commit): the Vulkan prefetch skips the same images.

Reviewed draft (verdict "ready with corrections"): gc-writeback-skip.v2.patch + .front.v2.patch.
One change to + lines, asked for: WritebackBandsCover's stub body (return false) is replaced by
the body the review gives (fault 4), 0565's TrySwizzleLayerInBands refusals that do not depend on
the guest range, so with both switches on the bands take what they can. live_switch.h re-anchored
after AheadGuardHeldAgeVerify; util.h/util.cpp re-anchored after 0565; all other +/- lines
byte-identical to the v2.
